\pard\nowidctlpar\li142\ri142\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qj\lang1033 This open-source application, developed in PureBasic for PureBasic programmers, lets you explore, understand, and refactor your ".pb" and ".pbi" source files as well as ".pbp" projects in depth. Should you wish to customize it or add your own features, its complete source code is available directly from the "Help and Tools" window.\par
Starting from a main file or project, PBBrowser reconstructs the exact compilation order of all included files (evaluating CompilerIf / CompilerSelect directives) and builds an instant inventory of procedures, macros, structures, interfaces, modules, variables, constants, enumerations, imports, and labels. With a single click, you can jump from one element to another, see who calls what, pinpoint where a variable is declared, modified, or tested, and immediately spot all unused project elements highlighted in gray.\par
PBBrowser also features a scope-aware Find / Replace engine (capable of safely renaming local or typed variables without false positives and searching multi-line complex expressions), along with a comprehensive built-in toolset: standalone single-file ".pb" exporter with surgical dead-code pruning, automatic "Declare" header and call-graph generator, "Protected" / unused local variable auditor, cosmetic code formatter, and ".pbp" project synchronizer.\par
Designed to work hand in hand with the PureBasic editor, PBBrowser installs in one click into the IDE's "Tools" menu (and uninstalls just as easily). Simply place the caret on any identifier in your code, press your chosen shortcut (CTRL + Q by default), and PBBrowser will instantly show everything there is to know about that element. Conversely, clicking a filename or line number in PBBrowser jumps straight to the exact line in the PureBasic editor. You can also freely test PBBrowser standalone and install it into the IDE later.\par
This message will not self-destruct: you can read it again at any time, along with practical tips and detailed documentation for every feature, by clicking the "Help and Tools" button.\f2\fs22\lang12\par
